<h1>Decimate</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span>Reduces the number of polygons while trying to preserve the quality of the selected mesh.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Parameters</b></span>:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><i style="font-style:italic;">Accuracy</i></b> – sets whether the optimisation to be by speed or accuracy. Range from 1 to 100. If Accuracy=1 optimisation is by speed. If Accuracy=100 optimisation is by accuracy. The intermediate values means optimisation either by speed and accuracy and the weight for each one depends on the particular value.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><i style="font-style:italic;">Method</i></b> – sets the method for polygon count reduction. Available options are: <i>3dDist</i> – decimation removes vertices from areas with less detail than the rest of the selected data set. This option decimates the data using the given number for tolerance. The tolerance represents distance from a point (that will be removed) to the surface formed by the neighbor points excluding the current point. <i>Pcent</i> – decreases the number of triangles in the selected data set by the percentage set for Pcent parameter. <i>MaxEdgeLength</i> – decreases the number of triangles of the selected data keeping each triangle edge length up to the value given to the MaxEdge parameter.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><i style="font-style:italic;">MaxDist</i></b> – 3D distance tolerance. Valid when Method=”3dDist”.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><i style="font-style:italic;">Pcent</i></b> – percentage of decreasing. Valid when Method=”Pcent”.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><i style="font-style:italic;">MaxEdge</i></b> – maximum edge length. Valid when Method=”MaxEdgeLength”.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><i style="font-style:italic;">RmBnd</i></b> – sets whether the triangles on the boundary of the object to be decimated or not. Available options are <i>Yes</i> and <i>No</i>.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>UI Commands</b></span>:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><i style="font-style:italic;">Mesh &gt; Polygon Reduction</i> from the main menu. <i>Tools &gt; Polygon Reduction</i> from the tree context menu for meshes. <b>&#160;Ctrl + D</b> shortcut.</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Examples:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode" style="font-family:Courier New;">Decimate( Accuracy=100, Method="3dDist", MaxDist=0.010, Pcent=50.000, MaxEdge=1000000.000, RmBnd=Yes )</p>
<p class="ExampleCode" style="font-family:Courier New;">Decimate( Accuracy=50, Method="Pcent", MaxDist=0.010, Pcent=50.000, MaxEdge=1000000.000, RmBnd=No )</p>
<p class="ExampleCode" style="font-family:Courier New;"><font style="font-family:Courier New;" face="Courier New">Decimate( Accuracy=0, Method="MaxEdgeLength", MaxDist=0.010, Pcent=100.000, MaxEdge=5.000, RmBnd=No )</font></p>
<p>&#160;</p>
